- The set of required points is  
  \[
  S_n=\{(a,b)\mid a,b\ge1,\ a+b\le n+1\}.
  \]
  For each integer \(a\) with \(1\le a\le n\) the column \(x=a\) contains the points \((a,1),\dots,(a,n+1-a)\).  
- The \(n\) vertical lines \(x=1, x=2,\dots, x=n\) are distinct and each line contains **all** points of its column, thus together they cover every point of \(S_n\).  

The solution does not spell out this argument; it merely states “Construction exists using vertical lines.”  
